{"task_id": "HumanEval/4", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef mean_absolute_deviation(numbers: List[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\" For a given list of input numbers, calculate Mean Absolute Deviation\n    around the mean of this dataset.\n    Mean Absolute Deviation is the average absolute difference between each\n    element and a centerpoint (mean in this case):\n    MAD = average | x - x_mean |\n    >>> mean_absolute_deviation([1.0, 2.0, 3.0, 4.0])\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty for MAD calculation.\")\n\n    # Calculate the mean of the input numbers.\n    x_mean = sum(numbers) / len(numbers)\n\n    # Calculate the absolute difference between each element and the mean.\n    absolute_differences = [abs(x - x_mean) for x in numbers]\n\n    # Calculate the average of the absolute differences.\n    mad_result = sum(absolute_differences) / len(absolute_differences)\n\n    return mad_result```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/5", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef intersperse(numbers: List[int], delimeter: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Insert a number 'delimeter' between every two consecutive elements of input list `numbers'.\n    Handles empty and single-element lists as specified.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not numbers:\n        return []\n    if len(numbers) == 1:\n        return numbers\n\n    result = [numbers[0]]\n    for i in range(1, len(numbers)):\n        result.append(delimeter)\n        result.append(numbers[i])\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "```python\ndef truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\" Given a positive floating point number, it can be decomposed into\n    and integer part (largest integer smaller than given number) and decimals\n    (leftover part always smaller than 1).\n\n    Return the decimal part of the number.\n    >>> truncate_number(3.5)\n    0.5\n    \"\"\"\n    integer_part = int(number)\n    decimal_part = number - integer_part\n    return decimal_part\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/3", "solution": "from typing import List\n\nclass BankAccount:\n    \"\"\"Manages the bank account balance and provides methods for updates and status checks.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initializes the bank account balance to zero.\"\"\"\n        self._balance: int = 0\n\n    def apply_operation(self, operation_value: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Updates the balance by adding the given operation value.\"\"\"\n        self._balance += operation_value\n\n    def is_below_zero(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the current balance is below zero.\"\"\"\n        return self._balance < 0\n\ndef below_zero(operations: List[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Detects if a bank account balance falls below zero at any point given a list of operations.\n    The account starts with a zero balance.\n    \"\"\"\n    account = BankAccount()\n    for op_value in operations:\n        account.apply_operation(op_value)\n        if account.is_below_zero():\n            return True\n    return False"}
