{"task_id": "HumanEval/36", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_divisible_by_11_or_13(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if number is divisible by 11 or 13.\"\"\"\n    return number % 11 == 0 or number % 13 == 0\n\ndef _count_digit_7(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts occurrences of the digit '7' in a number.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    s_number = str(number)\n    for digit in s_number:\n        if digit == '7':\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\ndef fizz_buzz(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return the number of times the digit 7 appears in integers less than n which are divisible by 11 or 13.\n    >>> fizz_buzz(50)\n    0\n    >>> fizz_buzz(78)\n    2\n    >>> fizz_buzz(79)\n    3\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sevens_count = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if _is_divisible_by_11_or_13(i):\n            total_sevens_count += _count_digit_7(i)\n    return total_sevens_count\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_cyclic function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # split string to groups. Each of length 3, same as encoding.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n    # reverse cycle elements in each group. Unless group has fewer elements than 3.\n    groups = [(group[-1] + group[:-1]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n    return \"\".join(groups)\n```"}
