{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _sort_list(numbers: list) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in ascending order.\"\"\"\n        return sorted(numbers)\n\n    def _get_middle_element(sorted_list: list):\n        \"\"\"Finds the middle element of a sorted list with an odd number of elements.\"\"\"\n        mid_index = len(sorted_list) // 2\n        return sorted_list[mid_index]\n\n    def _get_average_of_middle_elements(sorted_list: list) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the average of the two middle elements of a sorted list with an even number of elements.\"\"\"\n        mid_right_index = len(sorted_list) // 2\n        mid_left_index = mid_right_index - 1\n        return (sorted_list[mid_left_index] + sorted_list[mid_right_index]) / 2.0\n\n    def _determine_return_type(value: float):\n        \"\"\"Converts a float median to an integer if it has no fractional part, otherwise returns it as a float.\"\"\"\n        if value == int(value):\n            return int(value)\n        return value\n\n    sorted_list = _sort_list(l)\n\n    if len(sorted_list) % 2 == 1:\n        raw_median_value = _get_middle_element(sorted_list)\n    else:\n        raw_median_value = _get_average_of_middle_elements(sorted_list)\n\n    return _determine_return_type(float(raw_median_value))"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the last four values for fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3).\n    last_four = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = sum(last_four)\n        # Shift values: old fib4(i-3) becomes new fib4(i-4), etc.\n        last_four[0] = last_four[1]\n        last_four[1] = last_four[2]\n        last_four[2] = last_four[3]\n        last_four[3] = next_fib\n\n    return last_four[3]"}
