{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef _split_into_sentences(text, delimiters):\n    # Splits text into sentences based on delimiters, stripping whitespace.\n    escaped_delimiters = [re.escape(d) for d in delimiters]\n    delimiter_pattern = '|'.join(escaped_delimiters)\n    sentences_raw = re.split(f'([{delimiter_pattern}])', text)\n\n    processed_sentences = []\n    current_sentence = []\n    for part in sentences_raw:\n        if part in delimiters:\n            if current_sentence:\n                processed_sentences.append(''.join(current_sentence).strip() + part)\n            current_sentence = []\n        else:\n            current_sentence.append(part)\n\n    if current_sentence:\n        final_part = ''.join(current_sentence).strip()\n        if final_part:\n            processed_sentences.append(final_part)\n    return [s.strip() for s in processed_sentences if s.strip()]\n\ndef _starts_with_i(sentence):\n    # Determines if a sentence starts with the word \"I\", ignoring leading whitespace.\n    cleaned_sentence = sentence.strip()\n    return cleaned_sentence.startswith('I ') or cleaned_sentence == 'I'\n\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts sentences starting with \"I\". Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not S:\n        return 0\n\n    default_delimiters = ['.', '?', '!']\n    sentences = _split_into_sentences(S, default_delimiters)\n    boredom_count = 0\n    for sentence in sentences:\n        if _starts_with_i(sentence):\n            boredom_count += 1\n    return boredom_count\n```"}
